<title>USA: Advanced Digital stake cut by Vinik group.</title>
<headline>Advanced Digital stake cut by Vinik group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by former Fidelity Magellan Fund Manager Jeffery Vinik said Tuesday it cuts its stake in Advanced Digital Information Corp to 368,100 common shares or 4.6 percent from six percent previously held.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it sold 111,900 common shares between January 14 and January 20 at prices ranging from $19.5318 to $22.2015 per share.</p>
<p>The group holds the stake for investment purposes, the filing said.</p>
